## UniFi Controller Configuration (REQUIRED)
## Configure one or more UniFi controllers as a JSON array
## For UX7 and Dream Machine Pro controllers, use type="integrated"
## For standalone controllers, use type="standalone"

## Single Controller with Auto-Detection (Recommended for UX7)
UNIFI_CONTROLLERS=[{"url":"auto","username":"admin","password":"your_password","type":"integrated","siteIdentifier":"default","enabled":true}]

## Single Controller with Fixed URL
# UNIFI_CONTROLLERS=[{"url":"https://192.168.1.1","username":"admin","password":"your_password","type":"integrated","siteIdentifier":"default","enabled":true}]

## Multiple Controllers (Multi-Site Setup)
# UNIFI_CONTROLLERS=[{"url":"https://controller1.example.com","username":"admin1","password":"pass1","type":"standalone","siteIdentifier":"default","enabled":true},{"url":"https://controller2.example.com","username":"admin2","password":"pass2","type":"integrated","siteIdentifier":"site2","enabled":true}]

## Configuration Fields:
## - url: Controller URL or "auto" for automatic detection (optional, default: "auto")
## - username: Controller admin username (required)
## - password: Controller admin password (required)
## - type: "integrated" for UX7/Dream Machine or "standalone" for regular controllers (default: "integrated")
## - siteIdentifier: Site name in controller (default: "default")
## - enabled: true/false to enable/disable this controller (default: true)

## How Auto-Detection Works:
## When url is "auto" or omitted, the system detects the controller IP from:
## 1. Gateway query parameter (?gw=192.168.1.1)
## 2. HTTP Referer header (where the captive portal redirect originated)
## 3. X-UniFi-AP or X-UniFi-Controller custom headers
## 4. Redirect URL parameter

## Other Configuration
SESSION_SECRET=secretString
AUTH=none
REDIRECTURL=/success.html
NODE_ENV=production
PORT=80
